{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Release critique lens A2 (correctness and refusal safety) for the pending 8.9.5 patch","packet_sha256":"cf8bec24ffb7da50349880fef61f76f6e257ca525b4c425f47c1c583236a6dff","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"61980aa61e018101fb70232df87fea73a8a46e7fde7183a960ab68164cb6e20f","verdict":"block","target_observations":[{"target":"lane-target-declaration","verdict":"pass","summary":"The coverage floor is explicitly declared with --expected-target and remains independent of opaque packet labels.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review.py defines repeatable --expected-target separately from --prepared-target.","skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_execution.py derives expected_targets only from args.expected_target for both prompt construction and worker invocation.","tests/quality_gates/test_review_target_coverage_floor.py verifies that prepared-target labels alone retain shape-only behavior."]},{"target":"prepared-target-worker-wiring","verdict":"pass","summary":"Prompt and worker argv receive the same expected-target value, while prepared targets are not implicitly promoted into the floor.","evidence":["skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_execution.py passes getattr(args, \"expected_target\", None) to packet.write_prompt and passes the same value to invocation.runner_command.","skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_invocation.py emits one --expected-target argument for each supplied expected target.","skills/public/critique/scripts/run_review_packet.py sorts and deduplicates the prompt declaration, while the worker contract rejects duplicate argv declarations rather than approving them."]},{"target":"release-resume-notes-placeholder","verdict":"pass","summary":"Prepared-release resume packets preserve the notes-file requirement: one candidate is inserted, ambiguity is exposed as a placeholder, and absence emits no flag.","evidence":["skills/public/release/scripts/plan_release_run_packets.py selects the sole drafted note, emits <notes-file> for multiple candidates, and omits --notes-file only when no candidate exists.","tests/quality_gates/test_release_run_planner_prepared_stop.py exercises zero, one, and multiple drafted-note candidates and checks command and placeholder behavior.","The generated resume packets continue to list --notes-file among repeat_original_arguments."]},{"target":"staged-eviction-owner","verdict":"pass","summary":"The staged eviction gate precisely distinguishes a broad empty-universe refusal from an explicit selection containing no eviction-universe files, and the pre-commit dispatcher selects from the complete staged Python set.","evidence":["scripts/gates/check_module_eviction_form.py returns a clean no-op only when --paths was explicitly supplied and its intersection with the owned universe is empty; a broad empty scan still refuses.","scripts/hooks/check_staged_cheap_owners.py computes the eviction selection from staged_py_all rather than the code-length subset.","tests/quality_gates/test_module_eviction_form_gate.py covers broad empty refusal, explicit outside-universe no-op, and detection of a raw eviction in a selected test file."]},{"target":"task-run-persist-scope","verdict":"block","summary":"Persistence still permits a classification bypass: a candidate with changed_paths but no trustworthy disallowed-path classification is treated as fully admitted and committed.","evidence":["scripts/task_run/task_run_lane_runner.py::_in_scope_candidate_paths returns None only when changed_paths is not a list; otherwise it uses candidate.get(\"disallowed_paths\") or [] and therefore treats a missing or malformed falsey disallowed_paths value as an empty denied set.","scripts/task_run/task_run_completion.py refuses unscoped persistence only when _in_scope_candidate_paths returns None, so changed_paths alone bypasses the intended \"candidate classification unavailable\" refusal.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_completion.py tests missing changed_paths and a well-formed disallowed_paths list, but does not test changed_paths present with disallowed_paths absent or malformed."]},{"target":"worker-expected-targets","verdict":"pass","summary":"The worker enforces an explicitly declared floor after schema validation and binds that declaration through report, ledger, and provenance digests.","evidence":["skills/shared/scripts/run_reviewer_worker.py passes args.expected_target into finalize_attempt while the same declaration is parsed by the worker runner.","skills/shared/scripts/reviewer_result_contract.py requires exactly one nonempty observation for every expected target and distinguishes ReviewerCoverageError from schema failure.","skills/shared/scripts/reviewer_result_contract.py::require_joined_floor requires the report, ledger attempt, and provenance declaration digests to agree before revalidating the result.","tests/quality_gates/test_reviewer_runner.py covers declared refusal, declared success, and undeclared shape-only behavior."]}],"findings":[{"id":"A2-001","severity":"high","summary":"The unclassifiable-persist repair checks for changed-path presence, not for a usable scope classification.","evidence":["_in_scope_candidate_paths interprets any list-valued changed_paths as classified, even when disallowed_paths is absent.","A candidate such as {\"useful\": true, \"changed_paths\": [\"out-of-scope.py\"]} produces [\"out-of-scope.py\"] and reaches persist_incomplete_candidate instead of the fail-closed skip.","The persistence commit uses the returned paths directly, so the bypass can make an out-of-scope residue durable on the lane branch."],"action":"Require an explicit, well-formed scope-classification carrier before persistence—at minimum validate both changed_paths and disallowed_paths as lists produced by the scope verdict, or pass the admitted path set directly from the scope result. Add tests for missing, null, falsey malformed, and non-list disallowed_paths; each unclassifiable case must skip persistence and remain ineligible."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Explicit --paths bypasses the staged/worktree stability guard.","bin":"not-a-release-blocker","disposition":"The no-argument pre-commit path performs the stability check. Explicit paths are documented as deliberate worktree judgment and are used by tests and diagnostics; this is a separate API mode, not an evasion of the hook invocation shown in the packet."},{"concern":"Prepared-target labels do not automatically activate target coverage.","bin":"intended-opt-in","disposition":"The documentation, parser help, prompt construction, argv wiring, and tests consistently establish explicit --expected-target as the opt-in; opaque prepared-target membership remains backward compatible."},{"concern":"Prompt target order differs from argv declaration order.","bin":"safe-normalization","disposition":"The prompt uses a sorted set while the worker receives the original sequence. Order is semantically irrelevant, and duplicate argv declarations fail closed during expected-target normalization."},{"concern":"The staged module-eviction owner allows an explicit empty universe to pass.","bin":"precise-no-op","disposition":"This is correct for a path-scoped selection containing only files outside the owned universe; the broad scan retains its empty-universe refusal."},{"concern":"Resume notes placeholders could make a command look executable despite ambiguity.","bin":"adequately-signaled","disposition":"Ambiguity is represented in both the command and placeholders list, while execute packets still require user confirmation."}],"next_move":"Block 8.9.5 until task-run persistence requires a positive, well-formed scope classification when changed_paths is present, with regression tests proving missing or malformed classification cannot cause any path to be staged or committed. Then rerun this release critique against the repaired semantic input.","non_claims":["This review judges only the identity-bound inline payload and does not claim the current workspace matches it.","No tests or commands were executed, and no workspace files were edited.","The passing target observations do not override the task-run persistence blocker or make the patch safe to ship."]}
